          %title Books in algebraic geometry
          %h1#books_in_algebraic_geometry Books in algebraic geometry
          %p
            We should limit to books which we can really recommend, either by their special content, approach or pedagogical value. Historically fine but outdated books are in a separate historical section below. The outstanding surveys may be added to the lists if they are not too specialized to minor directions: the subfields may be covered in separate lists. See also MathOverflow discussions
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/2446/best-algebraic-geometry-text-book-other-than-hartshorne"} best-algebraic-geometry-text-book-other-than-hartshorne
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/61515/life-after-hartshorne-the-book-not-the-person"} life-after-hartshorne-the-book
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_algebraic_geometry"} Glossary of algebraic geometry
            is decent.
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#introductory_level_but_excellent_textbooks"} Introductory level but excellent textbooks
              %li
                %a{:href => "#schemes_standard_sources"} Schemes, standard sources
              %li
                %a{:href => "#grothendieck_school_sources"} Grothendieck school sources
              %li
                %a{:href => "#background_in_commutative_algebra"} Background in commutative algebra
              %li
                %a{:href => "#algebraic_groupsgroup_schemes_fouriermukai_transform"} Algebraic groups/group schemes; Fourier-Mukai transform
              %li
                %a{:href => "#complexanalytic_approach"} Complex-analytic approach
              %li
                %a{:href => "#mori_program_and_birational_geometry"} Mori program and birational geometry
              %li
                %a{:href => "#arithmetic_aspects"} Arithmetic aspects
              %li
                %a{:href => "#cohomology_theories_for_schemes"} Cohomology theories for schemes
              %li
                %a{:href => "#modern_extensions_of_scheme_theory"} Modern extensions of scheme theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#algorithmic_and_computational_methods"} Algorithmic and computational methods
              %li
                %a{:href => "#historically_important_but_now_outdated"} Historically important but now outdated
          %h2#introductory_level_but_excellent_textbooks Introductory level but excellent textbooks
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miles+Reid"}> Miles Reid
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Undergraduate algebraic geometry
              %strong 12
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joe+Harris"}> Joe Harris
              ,
              %em Introductory algebraic geometry
              (varieties)
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Shafarevich"}> Igor Shafarevich
              ,
              %em Basic algebraic geometry
              (varieties and schemes)
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeru+Mukai"}> Shigeru Mukai
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em An introduction to invariants and moduli
              %strong 81
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Fulton"}> William Fulton
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic curves. An introduction to algebraic geometry
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> J. S. Milne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic geometry
              %a{:href => "http://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/AG.pdf"} pdf
          %h2#schemes_standard_sources Schemes, standard sources
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Hartshorne"}> Robin Hartshorne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic geometry
            %li
              %p
                Qing Liu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic geometry and arithmetic curves
            %li
              %p
                D. Eisenbud, J. Harris,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of schemes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mumford"}> David Mumford
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Red book of varieties and schemes
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1358
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/b62130"} doi:10.1007/b62130
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (cf. also unfinished sequel notes for the later part of Mumford’s course, coauthored with Oda,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.math.upenn.edu/~chai/624_08/mumford-oda_chap1-6.pdf"} ch. 1-6 pdf
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.math.upenn.edu/~chai/624_08/mumford-oda_chap7-8.pdf"} ch. 7-8 pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Neeman"}> Amnon Neeman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic and analytic geometry
                %strong 345
            %li
              %p
                M. Demazure, P. Gabriel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Groupes algebriques
            %li
              %p
                Ravi Vakil’s Stanford
                %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/0708-216"} course notes
                or the more polished and recent
                %a{:href => "https://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/216blog/"} Rising Sea notes
            %li
              %p
                William Fulton,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Intersection theory
            %li
              %p
                Ulrich Görtz, Torsten Wedhorn,
                %em Algebraic Geometry I: Schemes
                With Examples and Exercises, 2nd Edition, Springer Studium Mathematik - Master, Springer Nature, 2020.
          %h2#grothendieck_school_sources Grothendieck school sources
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EGA"} EGA
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA"} SGA
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"}> FGA
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA+explained"} FGA explained
            %li
              R. Hartshorne,
              %em Residues and duality
            %li
              A. Grothendieck et al.
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dix exposes sur la cohomologie des schemas
